INSERT INTO public.companies (slug, name, subsector_id, website, chains, tags, meta)
SELECT v.slug, v.name, s.id, v.website, v.chains, v.tags, v.meta
FROM (VALUES
  ('swell-yield-vault-products', 'Swell (Yield Vault Products)', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'yield-structured-markets', 'https://www.swellnetwork.io', ARRAY['Medium (vault adoption dependent)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Yield vault products that deploy Swell’s staking assets into additional DeFi strategies to enhance returns beyond base staking.", "extras": {"Capital Lockups Typically none at vault level (withdrawal constraints can exist per strategy/asset conditions; check per vault) (yearn.fi) Typically none at vault level (vault-specific withdrawal mechanics apply; verify per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Typically none at vault level; withdrawal liquidity depends on upstream positions (verify per vault/strategy) (Harvest Finance) Maturity / term-structure is intrinsic (PT/YT exist “up to maturity”) (docs.pendle.finance) Yes (fixed term) — principal locked to maturity for PT holders (Delv Documentation) Yes (fixed term/maturity) (docs.notional.finance) Often epoch-like cycles (weekly) rather than free-form “anytime” yield; check per vault/product (docs.ribbon.finance) Often term-like “bond” framing (SMART Yield bonds) (lexology.com) Typically none strict, but tranche structure can imply different risk classes and coverage mechanics; validate per tranche": "Vault-specific (some strategies imply liquidity assumptions)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High upstream dependency stacking (Aave/Curve/Uni etc.); Medium governance/multisig execution concentration; Medium strategy-manager concentration (docs.yearn.fi) High upstream dependency stacking (LP farms + swap liquidity) • Medium strategy-maintainer concentration • Medium vault-level TVL concentration (docs.beefy.finance) High upstream dependency stacking • High strategy/implementation risk (vault-by-vault) • Medium governance/admin concentration risk (Harvest Finance) High dependency on supported yield-bearing collateral ecosystems; Medium governance/incentive concentration; Medium liquidity fragmentation risk across maturities (docs.pendle.finance) Medium dependency on underlying yield assets; Medium liquidity concentration risk in limited PT markets (Delv Documentation) Medium maturity liquidity concentration; Medium governance/risk-module dependency; Medium collateral/oracle valuation dependency (openzeppelin.com) High dependency on correct upgrade/oracle/settlement surfaces; Medium dependency on options liquidity regimes (theblock.co) Very High regulatory risk concentration; High governance/ops concentration; Medium dependency on underlying venues (lexology.com) High dependency on specific integrated venues per tranche; Medium governance/upgrade concentration; Medium liquidity/exit assumptions per tranche (docs.idle.finance)": "Medium–High dependency on specific DeFi venues; Medium governance concentration", "Downstream Consumers Retail vault depositors, DAO treasuries, structured products using yTokens, integrators sourcing yield Retail depositors, DAOs/treasuries seeking autocompounded exposure, integrators embedding vault yield Retail vault users, yield allocators, integrators (where applicable) Yield traders, DAOs/treasuries locking yield, structured product builders, hedgers/speculators Fixed-rate buyers (PT), variable yield seekers (YT), structured product builders (Delv Documentation) Fixed-income users (lend/borrow), LPs in maturity pools (nTokens), structured product builders referencing onchain rate curve Retail structured-yield users; DAOs via “Ribbon Treasury” style products (where applicable) (docs.ribbon.finance) Structured product participants; yield buyers seeking bond-like exposure Treasuries/DAOs and integrators seeking risk-adjusted yield via a single integration (idle.finance)": "Users seeking enhanced yield on top of Swell LST exposure", "Governance Model DAO governance with Multi-DAO workstreams + governance multisig execution layer (docs.yearn.fi) DAO governance (BIFI) + operational processes for strategy deployment (beefy.com) FARM governance + operational controls; docs also reference timelocks/controlled upgrades for strategy links (implementation-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Governance-driven incentives + parameter control (protocol-level) Governance/ops (protocol era-specific) Governance token (NOTE) + protocol ops Governance history + operational control surface (vault implementations + upgrades) (openzeppelin.com) DAO governance historically DAO governance": "Governance + protocol ops", "Historical Stress Behavior Battle-tested; stress typically manifests as strategy-specific losses/pauses and rapid reallocations rather than “bank-run” insolvency (validate per vault) (docs.yearn.fi) Stress manifests as upstream protocol issues, reward token volatility, or strategy/vault pauses; protocol docs emphasize autonomous contracts once deployed (operational continuity) (docs.beefy.finance) Notable exploit Oct 26, 2020 (~$24M) followed by large TVL outflows (“bank run” dynamic) (Nasdaq) Stress typically expresses as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) repricing of implied yields, not “vault insolvency” (docs.pendle.finance) Stress primarily appears as liquidity/market adoption constraints rather than protocol-driven yield failures (validate per term/market) (Delv Documentation) Stress tends to show up as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) collateral/risk parameter sensitivity rather than “strategy blowups” (docs.notional.finance) Dec 2025: legacy Ribbon DOV vaults reportedly drained (~$2.7M) after an oracle/upgrade-related issue (incident context) (theblock.co) Dec 22, 2023 SEC settlement impacted protocol operations and highlights structured-product regulatory sensitivity (lexology.com) Stress tends to surface as underlying market losses or tranche imbalance rather than “vault blowups” (evaluate per tranche/venue) (docs.idle.finance)": "Stress likely manifests as DeFi-venue exposure rather than staking failures", "Launch Year 2020 (YFI fair launch July 2020; iEarn origins Feb 2020) (CoinGecko) 2020 (vaults live Oct 8, 2020; origin Sept 2020) (docs.beefy.finance) 2020 (active protocol period; major exploit Oct 26, 2020) (Nasdaq) 2021 (V1 mainnet in June 2021) (Binance) 2021 (Ethereum mainnet launch June 30, 2021) (DELV) 2020 (V1; V2 later) (The Defiant) 2021 (Theta Vault era) (openzeppelin.com) 2020–2021 era (SMART Yield bonds/pools) (CoinGecko) 2019–2020 era (protocol matured into tranche suite by 2021) (Medium)": "2023", "Leverage Usage Conditional (some strategies may use leverage; vault-specific) Conditional (strategy-dependent; commonly no explicit leverage, but can include leveraged legs depending on vault design—validate per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Usually no explicit leverage; strategy-dependent (validate per strategy) (Harvest Finance) Can be enabled at product level (leverage and structured positioning common via integrations; validate per market/product) Not inherent; depends on integrations Can be used implicitly via borrowing/lending; leverage exists at user level (collateralized borrowing) Not inherent; users can lever externally (protocol itself primarily structures strategy exposure) Not inherent Generally no protocol-native leverage; users can lever externally": "Not inherent", "Maintaining Organization Yearn “Multi-DAO” structure: YFI holders + yTeams + Governance Multisig (execution / veto) (docs.yearn.fi) Beefy DAO (BIFI governance) + community contributors; vaults/strategies documented as autonomous smart contracts once deployed (docs.beefy.finance) Harvest contributors + FARM governance; strategy development guidance published in repo/docs (GitHub) Pendle contributors + governance (ve-style mechanics exist in protocol design; ops via core contributors) Delv / Element contributors (protocol + docs maintained by Delv) (Delv Documentation) Notional contributors + governance (NOTE; protocol ops) (Notional Finance) Ribbon / Aevo team + token governance history (structured vault system documented) (openzeppelin.com) BarnBridge DAO + founders/ops historically (structured product pools) (lexology.com) Idle DAO + contributors (product suite: Best Yield + Yield Tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "Swell team + governance", "Practitioner Validation Check YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs pass-through wrapper (Medium) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation/compounding • YES transformed yield vs passive wrapper (docs.beefy.finance) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs passive wrapper (Harvest Finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES transformed exposure (fixed/variable, duration) (docs.pendle.finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES fixed/variable exposures emerge from market structure (Delv Documentation) YES fixed/term transformation • YES programmatic market structure • PARTIAL multi-protocol dependency (more internal than Yearn/Pendle; still transforms yield) (docs.notional.finance) YES strategy transforms yield (premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) • YES automated program logic (openzeppelin.com) • YES not passive wrapper YES structured yield product using multi-protocol yield inputs (CoinGecko) • YES transforms exposure into bond/tranche form (lexology.com) YES multi-protocol strategy logic (docs.idle.finance) • YES programmatic allocation (GitHub) • YES transformed yield (tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "YES multi-protocol • YES programmatic strategy • YES yield transformed vs base staking", "Practitioner’s Note Diligence checklist: (1) which upstream protocols the vault touches, (2) strategy upgrade/admin controls, (3) keeper dependencies, (4) withdrawal liquidity assumptions under stress, (5) smart-contract/audit coverage per vault version (v2 vs v3). (docs.yearn.fi) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy contract risk (each vault is a different strategy), (2) reward token swap-path slippage/MEV, (3) upstream protocol risk (Curve/Convex/DEX LPs), (4) chain-bridge considerations if allocating cross-chain, (5) TVL concentration by a few flagship vaults. (docs.beefy.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) per-vault strategy complexity, (2) reliance on Curve/LP mechanics (historically relevant), (3) upgrade/timelock and admin controls, (4) withdrawal assumptions under stress, (5) post-incident security posture and audits. (Least Authority) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity and implied rate curve behavior, (2) oracle/market pricing assumptions for PT/YT, (3) liquidity depth around maturity, (4) underlying yield source risk (what generates the yield), (5) incentive/governance concentration risk. (docs.pendle.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity/term risk, (2) PT discount mechanics (fixed rate only if PT bought at discount), (3) liquidity depth in PT markets, (4) underlying yield asset assumptions. (Delv Documentation) Boundary caution: Notional sits near Lending Markets. Classify here when your analysis is about rate curve / maturity markets (fCash) and yield transformation; classify in Lending when focusing on credit creation and collateral rules. (docs.notional.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy payoff under spot/vol regime shifts, (2) vault parameter/upgrade controls, (3) settlement/oracle upgrade risk, (4) liquidity/withdrawal mechanics by epoch, (5) tail-risk events (vault drains / contract issues). (theblock.co) Risk flags dominate: (1) regulatory enforcement precedent (SEC), (2) governance/ops centralization risk, (3) underlying venue concentration, (4) product run-off / deprecation risk, (5) liquidity/exit constraints for bond-like products. (lexology.com) Diligence checklist: (1) what the tranche’s underlying strategy venue is, (2) coverage mechanics (how junior absorbs losses), (3) concentration in a single underlying market, (4) oracle/venue liquidation behavior, (5) governance/upgrade controls. (docs.idle.finance)": "Boundary clarity: Swell LST belongs in the LST subsector. Only classify here when analyzing vault-level yield engineering.", "Principal Protection None (no guaranteed principal protection; depends on upstream protocols) None None None (no guaranteed principal protection; PT value depends on underlying + market discount) None (economic “fixed rate” comes from PT discount; no guarantee beyond underlying solvency) (Delv Documentation) None (protocol enforces redemption mechanics; principal depends on protocol solvency/market + collateral rules) None (strategy risk is explicit; drawdowns possible) (openzeppelin.com) Not guaranteed; product framing implies structured payoffs but depends on underlying + pool rules Conditional (Senior has built-in protection via Junior counterparty, within tranche design limits) (docs.idle.finance)": "None", "Protocol Status Active (Vaults, including V3 allocator vault architecture) (docs.yearn.fi) Active (multi-chain; Ethereum-supported vaults) (docs.beefy.finance) Active (vault/strategy architecture documented; Ethereum focus in docs) (Harvest Finance) Active Historical / reduced activity (kept for design relevance: PT/YT fixed-income design) (Delv Documentation) Active (focus here: fixed-rate yield structuring via fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Legacy structured vaults exist; operational context changed (rebrand + legacy vault incident Dec 2025) (theblock.co) Constrained / high regulatory risk (SEC settlement Dec 2023 on SMART Yield) (lexology.com) Active": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Fits criteria: abstracts/aggregates yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, transforms exposure via vault strategy logic (not a single primitive). (Medium) Fits criteria: abstracts yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, and transforms exposure via automated compounding/position management. (docs.beefy.finance) Fits criteria: programmatic strategy logic deploying capital across multiple protocols; transformed yield exposure via autocompounding and strategy routing. (Harvest Finance) Fits criteria: transforms yield exposure (fixed/variable) and depends on multi-protocol yield sources + programmatic tokenization/market logic. (docs.pendle.finance) Fits criteria: transformed yield exposure via PT/YT engineering and multi-protocol yield inputs; included explicitly as historical/design-relevant. (Delv Documentation) Included only for the yield-structuring component: it transforms yield into a term structure (fixed-rate markets) rather than simply sourcing yield from one primitive. (docs.notional.finance) Fits criteria: yield is engineered and transformed via strategy logic (options-selling) rather than sourced from a single primitive. (docs.ribbon.finance) Fits criteria: yield depends on multi-protocol aggregation and structured payoff logic, not a single primitive. (CoinGecko) Fits criteria: abstracts yield across protocols and transforms exposure via tranching (risk-adjusted yield products). (docs.idle.finance)": "Included only at the vault layer: yield is derived from multi-protocol strategy logic, not from the base LST itself.", "Rebalancing Logic Strategy-defined (periodic + event-driven; allocator discretion in V3) (docs.yearn.fi) Event-driven/periodic compounding via harvest() workflows in strategies (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy-defined harvesting/compounding cycles (periodic + event-driven) (Harvest Finance) Market-driven; maturity-based lifecycle (PT/YT converge to maturity; AMM liquidity + solver/LP behavior) (docs.pendle.finance) Maturity-driven; PT redemption at term, YT captures differential yield (Delv Documentation) Maturity-based: fCash redeems at face value at maturity; trading implies fixed rate (docs.notional.finance) Periodic (weekly options cycles) (docs.ribbon.finance) Term-/pool-structure driven (bond-like) Periodic / event-driven (strategy-dependent)": "Periodic / strategy-defined", "Risk Transformation Optimization + risk-adjusted routing (yield abstraction; not classic tranching by default) (Medium) Optimization (autocompounding + routing to underlying farms/LPs) (docs.beefy.finance) Optimization (routes to underlying protocols + compounds) (Harvest Finance) Duration + yield separation (turns yield into a tradable component; enables fixed-rate via PT discounting) (docs.pendle.finance) Duration transformation + yield separation (zero-coupon style via discounted PT) (Delv Documentation) Duration transformation (creates fixed-term claims, fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Volatility → yield transformation (systematically converts vol risk into premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) Risk tranching / structured finance (bonds/pools segment exposure) (lexology.com) Risk transformation (Senior/Junior tranches): senior gets protection, junior takes first loss for boosted yield (docs.idle.finance)": "Yield aggregation above LST (combines staking + DeFi yield legs)", "Strategy Change Control Governance-/manager-approved strategy onboarding and parameterization (allocator vault “plug & play” with manager choice) (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy/vault additions are gated by protocol processes (strategy contracts define capital deployment logic) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy changes are controlled via protocol mechanisms (vault↔strategy linkage and upgrade controls), strategy development guided in repo/docs (GitHub) Governance/ops controls which markets/assets are supported and how incentives are allocated Admin/governance selects supported assets/terms and contract deployments Governance controls risk params/markets and upgrades (per governance processes) Strategy params and vault operations are not “set-and-forget” immutable; validate admin/upgrade controls per deployment (openzeppelin.com) Strategy/product operation and ongoing maintenance were treated as operationally controlled (per enforcement narratives) (klgates.com) Strategy integrations guided by a documented risk framework; additions/changes are governance/ops-mediated (docs.idle.finance)": "Vault strategies governed and upgraded via protocol controls", "Strategy Management Mixed: strategy authors + vault managers; governance/ops oversight via Multi-DAO + multisig execution (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy contracts + DAO-approved strategy framework (practically: contributors maintain strategy library) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy contracts (explicitly described as defining how vault funds are used in 3rd party protocols) (Harvest Finance) Programmatic yield tokenization + AMM markets; governance directs incentives/market support Programmatic tokenization + AMM markets for PT/YT Protocol-defined market structure (maturities, fCash issuance/redemption rules) (docs.notional.finance) Automated strategy vaults (rule-based; typically weekly cadence) (docs.ribbon.finance) Protocol-defined structuring (bonds/pools) with governance/ops historically involved (klgates.com) Algorithmic allocation + productized tranche mechanics; risk framework for integrating new markets (docs.idle.finance)": "Protocol-managed vault strategies", "Strategy Scope Multi-protocol (core design) Multi-protocol (per-vault strategies allocate into LPs/farms and reinvest rewards) (docs.beefy.finance) Multi-protocol (vault funds deployed into 3rd party protocols via strategies) (Harvest Finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield-bearing assets across DeFi) (docs.pendle.finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield assets) Primarily internal markets (Notional-native pools); upstream yield legs can include cToken-style yield for LPs (implementation-dependent) (Medium) Multi-protocol (vault logic + options infrastructure + settlement) Multi-protocol (aggregates yield from underlying venues and re-slices into structured tranches/bonds) (CoinGecko) Multi-protocol (allocates across integrated markets; tranche strategies point to underlying venues) (docs.idle.finance)": "Multi-protocol (vaults deploy swETH/LRTs into DeFi strategies)", "Underlying Yield Sources Lending (Aave/Compound), LP positions (Curve/Uni/Balancer), incentives, other DeFi yield legs (strategy-dependent) (Medium) LP fees (DEXs), lending yield (where used), incentive rewards (farm tokens), CLM where applicable (docs.beefy.finance) Lending yield, LP fees, incentive rewards (strategy-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Yield-bearing tokens (e.g., lending receipts, LSTs, incentive-bearing wrappers), rewards streams (asset-dependent) (docs.pendle.finance) Yield-bearing assets (lending receipts, LP-like yield assets depending on supported integrations) Fixed-rate lending/borrowing; LP yield from pool fees + underlying interest sources (nToken context) (Medium) Options premium (systematic selling), sometimes paired with lending/treasury products (product-dependent) (docs.ribbon.finance) Aggregated yield from “different protocols” per overviews of SMART Yield concept (CoinGecko) Lending markets / strategy venues integrated into Best Yield + Tranches (per-asset strategy) (docs.idle.finance)": "Staking yield, restaking yield, DeFi yield (lending/LP depending on vault)", "Upstream Dependencies Lending markets, DEXs/LP venues, oracles (indirect), keeper networks, bridges/LP gauges (strategy-dependent) (Medium) DEXs (Uniswap/Curve/etc.), farm platforms (Convex-style), token swap liquidity for compounding, chain-specific infra (docs.beefy.finance) 3rd party protocols (Curve/lending/DEXs), price/liquidity conditions for safe unwinds, keeper/executor processes (Harvest Finance) Tokenization contracts (SY/PT/YT), AMM liquidity engines, underlying protocols that generate yield (lending, staking/LSTs, etc.) (docs.pendle.finance) Tokenization contracts, AMM liquidity, underlying yield sources Native liquidity pools, collateral valuation + risk modules; oracle/valuation surfaces are a key diligence item (audit trail exists) (openzeppelin.com) Options infrastructure / vault contracts; relies on settlement correctness and any price/oracle upgrade surfaces relevant to vaults (theblock.co) Underlying yield venues; governance/ops controls; legal/compliance constraints now primary practical dependency (lexology.com) Underlying lending/strategy markets (e.g., Instadapp-based strategies in examples), oracles/keepers indirectly via venues (docs.idle.finance)": "Base LSTs/LRTs, DeFi venues (Aave-like, Curve-like), oracle layers", "Yield Model Aggregated + strategy vaults (optimized yield) Aggregated + autocompounding optimizer Aggregated yield vaults + autocompounding Structured / transformed yield (separates yield vs principal; enables fixed/variable exposure via PT/YT) (docs.pendle.finance) Structured yield (splits yield-bearing assets into Principal Tokens + Yield Tokens; fixed/variable via market pricing) (Delv Documentation) Fixed / term yield via fCash pricing in native liquidity pools (docs.notional.finance) Structured yield (options-selling “theta” style) Structured / tranched yield (SMART Yield) Aggregated + risk-tranching structured yield": "Aggregated / structured yield (vault layer)"}, "source_label": "Yield & Structured Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('lido', 'Lido', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'liquid-staking-tokens', 'https://lido.fi', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A liquid staking protocol that pools ETH to run validators and issues stETH, a liquid, rebasing token representing a claim on Ethereum consensus staking rewards.", "extras": {"Accepted as Collateral": "Widely accepted (Aave, Maker, many others)", "Claim Type": "Pro-rata claim on pooled ETH validator rewards", "DEX Liquidity Depth": "Deep (one of the deepest LST markets)", "Dependency Concentration Risk": "High reliance on a small set of operators and major liquidity venues", "Exit Liquidity Risk": "Medium (market liquidity + withdrawal queues during stress)", "Governance Centralization Risk": "Medium (DAO governance with concentrated voting power)", "Governance Model": "DAO (LDO)", "Historical Stress Behavior": "2022 market stress saw stETH trade at a discount to ETH; liquidity normalized over time post-withdrawals enablement", "LST Token Name": "stETH", "Launch Year": "2020", "Maintaining Organization": "Lido DAO (token holders) with a Node Operator set", "Oracle Availability": "Widely supported (price feeds/TWAPs)", "Practitioner Validation Check": "YES consensus-layer staking claim • YES transferable liquid token • YES DeFi composable without unstaking", "Practitioner’s Note": "Watchpoints: validator set concentration, governance power over operators, stETH↔ETH liquidity during stress, and how slashing/penalties propagate to holders.", "Primary Liquidity Venues": "Curve (stETH/ETH), Uniswap; centralized venues support varies", "Protocol Status": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion": "Meets criteria: issues a liquid, transferable ETH staking representation tied directly to consensus rewards and usable across DeFi without unstaking.", "Rebasing Model": "Rebasing (balance increases with staking rewards)", "Redemption Mechanism": "Protocol-level withdrawal queue (post-Shanghai) + secondary market liquidity", "Slashing Risk Bearer": "Token holders ultimately bear slashing via reduced rewards/principal; mitigated by operator insurance & monitoring", "Systemic Importance": "High (largest LST; core collateral across DeFi)", "Token Standard": "ERC-20 (rebasing)", "Upgrade / Admin Controls": "Governance-controlled upgrades; contracts not immutable", "Validator Concentration Risk": "Medium–High (permissioned operator set)", "Validator Operator Model": "Permissioned node operators (professional validators)", "Validator Selection & Governance": "Node Operators approved/removed by Lido DAO governance; curated set"}, "source_label": "Liquid Staking Tokens (LSTs)"}'::jsonb),
  ('rocket-pool', 'Rocket Pool', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'liquid-staking-tokens', 'https://rocketpool.net', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A decentralized liquid staking protocol issuing rETH, a non-rebasing token whose exchange rate to ETH increases with staking rewards from permissionless validators.", "extras": {"Accepted as Collateral": "Broad but more selective than stETH (Aave, Maker via parameters, others)", "Claim Type": "Pro-rata claim on pooled ETH validator rewards", "DEX Liquidity Depth": "Moderate–Deep", "Dependency Concentration Risk": "Medium reliance on DEX liquidity; Medium reliance on RPL token economics", "Exit Liquidity Risk": "Medium (smaller liquidity than stETH; redemption latency applies)", "Governance Centralization Risk": "Low–Medium (DAO governs parameters, not operator selection)", "Governance Model": "DAO (RPL)", "Historical Stress Behavior": "Traded near parity during stress; smaller but resilient liquidity compared to stETH", "LST Token Name": "rETH", "Launch Year": "2021", "Maintaining Organization": "Rocket Pool DAO + permissionless node operators", "Oracle Availability": "Widely supported (core DeFi oracles)", "Practitioner Validation Check": "YES consensus-layer staking claim • YES transferable • YES DeFi composable", "Practitioner’s Note": "Watchpoints: minipool health, RPL bond dynamics, validator churn, and rETH liquidity relative to stETH during market stress.", "Primary Liquidity Venues": "Uniswap, Balancer; secondary market venues", "Protocol Status": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion": "Meets criteria: liquid ETH staking token directly tied to Ethereum consensus rewards and usable across DeFi without unstaking.", "Rebasing Model": "Non-rebasing (exchange rate increases vs ETH)", "Redemption Mechanism": "Protocol-level redemption (subject to validator exits) + secondary market", "Slashing Risk Bearer": "Primarily node operators via bonded RPL + socialized risk to rETH holders in extreme cases", "Systemic Importance": "High (second canonical LST; decentralization benchmark)", "Token Standard": "ERC-20 (non-rebasing)", "Upgrade / Admin Controls": "Governance-controlled upgrades; protocol parameters adjustable", "Validator Concentration Risk": "Low–Medium (permissionless operator set reduces concentration)", "Validator Operator Model": "Permissionless (any operator can run a minipool with bonded RPL)", "Validator Selection & Governance": "Protocol-defined rules; operators are not DAO-curated; DAO governs parameters"}, "source_label": "Liquid Staking Tokens (LSTs)"}'::jsonb),
  ('coinbase', 'Coinbase', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'liquid-staking-tokens', 'https://www.coinbase.com', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A custodial liquid staking token representing ETH staked by Coinbase, with rewards accruing via an increasing cbETH/ETH exchange rate.", "extras": {"Accepted as Collateral": "Accepted with conservative parameters in select protocols", "Claim Type": "Custodial claim on ETH staked by Coinbase on behalf of users", "DEX Liquidity Depth": "Moderate", "Dependency Concentration Risk": "High reliance on Coinbase operations, policy, and liquidity venues", "Exit Liquidity Risk": "Medium–High (liquidity + custodial policy dependency)", "Governance Centralization Risk": "High (centralized issuer control)", "Governance Model": "Centralized corporate governance", "Historical Stress Behavior": "cbETH has traded at discounts during periods of market stress and regulatory uncertainty", "LST Token Name": "cbETH", "Launch Year": "2022", "Maintaining Organization": "Coinbase (centralized exchange & custodian)", "Oracle Availability": "Widely supported (major oracle providers)", "Practitioner Validation Check": "YES consensus-layer staking claim • YES transferable • YES DeFi usable without unstaking", "Practitioner’s Note": "Watchpoints: custodial risk, regulatory exposure, validator concentration, and reliance on Coinbase’s operational continuity.", "Primary Liquidity Venues": "Uniswap, Curve (limited), centralized exchange venues", "Protocol Status": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion": "Meets criteria: liquid, transferable token representing Ethereum consensus staking yield.", "Rebasing Model": "Non-rebasing (exchange rate increases vs ETH)", "Redemption Mechanism": "Market-based liquidity; protocol redemption subject to Coinbase staking/withdrawal policies", "Slashing Risk Bearer": "Coinbase + token holders (users exposed to operator/custodial risk)", "Systemic Importance": "High (major exchange-issued LST; significant validator share)", "Token Standard": "ERC-20 (non-rebasing)", "Upgrade / Admin Controls": "Admin-gated (issuer-controlled contracts/policies)", "Validator Concentration Risk": "High (single operator)", "Validator Operator Model": "Centralized / custodial (Coinbase-operated validators)", "Validator Selection & Governance": "Validator operations and policies controlled internally by Coinbase"}, "source_label": "Liquid Staking Tokens (LSTs)"}'::jsonb),
